The issue is that neither `../../../common/mc.h` nor `<ap_int.h>` are available in this compilation environment. Since the wide bus approach requires HLS-specific headers that aren't available for standalone C++ compilation, the smallest fix is to revert the function signature back to the original `double*` interface while keeping all the other optimizations (pipeline, unroll, double-buffering, tiling, array partitioning) intact. The m_axi interface with burst settings still provides memory coalescing benefit through the HLS INTERFACE pragmas.

